# Module 1 - Governance and Compliance

## Governance
- Defines cybersecurity accountability
- Aligns security with business goals
- Helps manage cyber risks

## Important Roles
### Data Owner
Responsible for data ownership and classification.

### Data Custodian
Maintains and protects systems storing data.

### Data Protection Officer
Ensures privacy law compliance.

## Cybersecurity Policies
- Password Policy
- Acceptable Use Policy
- Remote Access Policy
- Incident Handling Policy

## Human Resources Security

- Security awareness training helps prevent phishing attacks.
- User access controls enforce the need-to-know principle.
- IDS/IPS monitoring helps detect unauthorized software downloads.
- Monitor abnormal employee behavior to identify policy violations.

## Key Takeaway
Strong governance, security policies, and user controls help organizations protect data, reduce cyber risks, and maintain compliance.
